-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/7e1fa3fe-03de-5519-8457-2bb42e5ecea1
-- title:
--   q-adic cusp place centred at a good point, q=3
-- statement:
--   The ambient data are a prime $q$ together with the hypothesis `hq3 : q = 3`, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Two function fields occur: $\bar F_{M'} =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the subfield of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, and $F =$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, the corresponding geometric field at level $q^2M'$ with level subgroup `levelH q M'` (the kernel of the unit-group reduction attached to the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'`); `hle` asserts $\bar F_{M'} \le F$. On the residue side, `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is the subfield of Laurent series over `ResidueField A` generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` is given, and `hW` says that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`, the set of elements $j$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve with $j$-invariant $j$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Here a `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$, whose ideals are principal; `ord`, `evalAt` and `IsRational` are its order function, its residue value in $K$ (defined via the inverse of the structure map on residue fields), and the surjectivity of $K \to$ residue field.
--
--   The reduction data are: a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ for $A$ from $\bar F_{M'}$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\bar F_{M'}$, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, inducing on constants the residue map of $A$, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisor pushforward), and the hypothesis `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $\bar F_{M'}$, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. A primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` is fixed.
--
--   Two families of valuation subrings of $F$ are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), the projective line over $\mathbb{Z}/q$, and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ at the point `lineInfty q` as the ring of those $f \in F$ for which there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with the reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ after coefficientwise inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; `hIg`, which for each point $\ell$ of the projective line produces $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = ℓ` and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ equal to the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ gives a permutation $\sigma$ of the projective line with $(O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell))$ pulled back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\sigma \ell)$ for all $\ell$.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that a constant $x \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ if and only if $x \in A$; `hSS_over`, which for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ is regular at every place of $\bar F_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the element of $\bar F_{M'}$ given by the $q$-expansion `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of the modular invariant is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, asserts both that the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and that for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and the constant $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t$ minus any constant from $A$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there. Further, $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` for $A$ from $F$ to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (valuation subring, surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, with the scaling property `exists_smul_mem`), with `hR : R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O` says that $f \in \bar F_{M'}$ lies in `R₀.integers` precisely when its image in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   The arithmetic of the base is encoded by: an element $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cap A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; a subfield $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that the valuation ring $A \cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hdvr`, `hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), together with `hκ`, the condition that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$; an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; and finally a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ whose elements are exactly those of $K_1$ lying in $A$, $A_1$ being a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated with $F$ viewed as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and is universally quantified over a $k_0$-subfield $F_0$ of $F$ subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by all constants from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of $F$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness condition, namely for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants from $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and $F_0$ contains every element of $F$ whose underlying Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`.
--
--   Put $T_1$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the constants from $K_1$. The statement is further quantified over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map sends $a \in A_1$ to the constant image of $a \in K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in $F$, and over an element $j_1 \in T_1$, nonzero, whose image in $F$ is the inclusion along `hle` of the element of $\bar F_{M'}$ given by `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq`. Over these data the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X}_1 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is formed: the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` (the elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$.
--
--   Three auxiliary notions are introduced for $x \in \mathfrak{X}_1$ and $f \in T_1$. `InStalk x f` holds when, for every point $y$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` mapping to $x$ under `ιFin`, there are $g, h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for every point $y$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf` over $x$ with `ιInf` and `chartAlgInf`. `InMax x f` is the same statement with the additional requirement $g \in y$ in both clauses. For a place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, `Centred P x` holds when $P$ is rational and, for every $f \in T_1$ with `InStalk x f`, the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ lies in $A$, and the $A$-valuation of that value is $< 1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. Finally `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; the only specialisation of $x$ is $x$ itself; for every point $y$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` over $x$, every $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` whose image in $F$ is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in $y$; the same for $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf` and `chartAlgInf`; and for every point $y$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   The assertion is then: there exists a place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose valuation subring is `qIntegersBar (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M')`, the ring of elements of $F$ whose Laurent series has order $\ge 0$, and there exists a point $x$ of $\mathfrak{X}_1$ such that `GoodPt x` and `Centred P x` both hold.
--
--   This is the statement, for $q = 3$, that the cusp $\infty$ of the geometric level-$q^2M'$ modular function field — the place given by non-negative order of the $q$-expansion — is centred at a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model which lies on the $\infty$-Igusa branch and is not supersingular. It feeds the construction of the smooth Igusa base model, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three).
